 When a ceiling is reached TA stops the agent, prints which ceiling and what was used, records the outcome `aborted_budget` on the goal, and builds the draft from the partial work, marked as incomplete (`ta draft view` says so first). What it can promise: TA reads the runtime's usage report after each agent turn, so the agent is stopped at the first turn boundary after the ceiling is crossed. Overshoot is possible by up to one turn (a single long turn can cost a lot); undershoot is capped, since a goal is never stopped before it reaches the ceiling. Ceilings are enforced only for headless runs, because that is where TA reads the usage report. `--max-usd` needs a price: from the runtime's reported cost or the price table. For an unpriced model it warns and only `--max-tokens` applies. A goal that finishes on its own over the ceiling is not marked incomplete.
 
+### Reporting spend across goals and interactive sessions
+
+`GET /api/spend` only sees TA goals, but long interactive Claude Code and OMP sessions are often the larger bill. `ta cost report` puts all three in one table:
+
+```bash
+ta cost report                                   # one row per source
+ta cost report --since 2026-10-01 --group-by day,source
+ta cost report --group-by context_bucket         # where the cache-read money goes
+ta cost report --project TrustedAutonomy --group-by model --json
+```
+
+It reads each source that exists on the machine and says which it found:
+
+| Source | Where | Notes |
+|---|---|---|
+| `ta_goals` | this project's goal records | Same numbers as `/api/spend` (uses the same aggregator) |
+| `claude_code` | `~/.claude/projects/**/*.jsonl` | Priced from the price table: an estimate |
+| `omp` | `~/.omp/agent/sessions/**/*.jsonl` | OMP's own recorded cost: exact |
+
+Flags: `--since` and `--until` (a date or an RFC 3339 time, UTC), `--project` (part of a project name, any case), `--group-by` (any of `day`, `source`, `model`, `project`, `context_bucket`, `origin_class`, comma-separated), `--json`. `origin_class` applies to goals only; transcript rows show `n/a`.
+
+Example output:
+
+```text
+ta cost report
+Range: all time (UTC)
+Sources:
+  missing ta_goals     not found: .../.ta/goals does not exist, so no TA goals are counted (this is not an error; ...)
+  found   claude_code  5665 file(s), 52021 turn(s) counted after deduplicating by message id
+          48046 duplicate row(s) removed; 85 <synthetic> row(s) skipped; 15419 row(s) from TA goal sessions left out (...)
+  found   omp          133 file(s), 12147 turn(s) counted
+Costs: 12147 exact, 16625 estimated, 35396 unpriced (no price for the model: tokens counted, usd 0)
+
+  SOURCE       ITEMS  INPUT   OUTPUT  CACHE READ  CACHE WRITE  USD      EXACT/EST/UNPRICED
+  claude_code  52021  113.3k  29.5M   16829.8M    416.9M       4968.44  0/16625/35396
+  omp          12147  40.7k   9.9M    1348.7M     38.2M        387.00   12147/0/0
+  TOTAL        64168  154.0k  39.4M   18178.5M    455.2M       5355.43  12147/16625/35396
+
+Context size per turn (transcript sources):
+  SOURCE       CONTEXT   TURNS  CACHE READ  USD
+  claude_code  0-50k     2836   86.7M       194.12
+  claude_code  >400k     17764  11678.7M    1847.56
+  ...
+```
+
+How to read it:
+
+- **Context size.** The second table splits turns by how large the prompt was (fresh input plus cache read plus cache write): 0 to 50k, 50 to 100k, 100 to 200k, 200 to 400k and over 400k tokens. A turn's cache-read cost grows with its context, so a few very long sessions can dominate the bill. It is always printed, for each transcript source.
+- **Counting.** Claude Code repeats a message's row while streaming, so rows are deduplicated by message id (the last row wins) and `<synthetic>` rows are skipped. The header says how many were removed.
+- **1 hour cache writes.** When a transcript splits cache writes into 5 minute and 1 hour classes, the 1 hour part is priced at 2 times the input price. A `cache_write_1h` line in a `.ta/pricing.toml` row overrides that rate.
+- **Exact, estimated, unpriced.** A cost is exact when the runtime or OMP reported it, estimated when it was priced from the table, and unpriced when the table has no row for the model. Unpriced turns keep their tokens and show 0.00; TA never guesses a price. Add the model to `.ta/pricing.toml` to price it.
+- **Goal sessions.** A Claude Code session that `ta run` started in `.ta/staging/` is already a goal record, so it is left out of `claude_code` to avoid counting it twice. Pass `--include-goal-sessions` to count it anyway.
+- **Missing sources.** A source directory that does not exist is listed as `missing` in the header and the report carries on with the rest.
